        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/peterchayward/{size}/2098_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-09-03T16:15:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>when you attack another clone while overwhelm-people's hammer and a new clone comes into play, does the new clone get to use people's hammer from overwhelm?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I'm not official, but unless the wording on Overwhelm is an exception, I'm going to say definitely not. Like attacks, you declare targets and then the action is carried out based on those targets.</p>",
